= Understanding the VCD File
VCD stands for *Value Change Dump*. A VCD file records changes in digital signals during simulation.
The VCD file can be opened using GTKWave.

= Automating the Process with GNU Make
Typing the complete GHDL commands manually becomes inconvenient as a project becomes larger. For
example, every time the design is changed, we would need to execute:

```bash
ghdl -a --std=08 -fexplicit -frelaxed-rules --syn-binding ./src/alu.vhd
ghdl -a --std=08 -fexplicit -frelaxed-rules --syn-binding ./tb/tb_alu.vhd
ghdl -e --std=08 -fexplicit -frelaxed-rules --syn-binding -o ./bin/tb_alu tb_alu
ghdl -r --std=08 -fexplicit -frelaxed-rules --syn-binding tb_alu \
    --vcd=./bin/tb_alu.vcd --stop-time=200ns
```

We can automate these commands using a `Makefile`. Create:
```bash
touch Makefile
```

Add:
```makefile
TOP = tb_alu
SRC = ./src/alu.vhd
TB  = ./tb/tb_alu.vhd

GHDL_FLAGS = --std=08 -fexplicit -frelaxed-rules --syn-binding

compile:
	mkdir -p ./bin
	ghdl -a $(GHDL_FLAGS) $(SRC)
	ghdl -a $(GHDL_FLAGS) $(TB)
	ghdl -e $(GHDL_FLAGS) -o ./bin/$(TOP) $(TOP)

run:
	ghdl -r $(TOP) --vcd=./bin/$(TOP).vcd --stop-time=200ns

wave:
	gtkwave ./bin/$(TOP).vcd

clean:
	rm -rf ./bin/$(TOP)
	rm -f ./bin/$(TOP).vcd
	rm -f work-obj08.cf
```

The commands underneath each target must begin with a *tab character*, not spaces.

= Using the Makefile
The Makefile provides four targets.

== Compile
Run:
```bash
make compile
```

This performs analysis of both VHDL files and elaborates the testbench. It is equivalent to:
```bash
ghdl -a --std=08 -fexplicit -frelaxed-rules --syn-binding ./src/alu.vhd
ghdl -a --std=08 -fexplicit -frelaxed-rules --syn-binding ./tb/tb_alu.vhd
ghdl -e --std=08 -fexplicit -frelaxed-rules --syn-binding -o ./bin/tb_alu tb_alu
```

== Run
Run:
```bash
make run
```

This executes the simulation. The waveform is generated as:
```text
bin/tb_alu.vcd
```

== View the Waveform
Run:
```bash
make wave
```

== Clean
Run:
```bash
make clean
```

This removes generated simulation files.

