= Simulation Versus FPGA Implementation
One of the most important concepts to understand is that *simulation is not the same as FPGA
implementation*.

In this lab, we are only simulating the VHDL design.

No FPGA is required.

No bitstream is generated.

No physical hardware is programmed.

= Important GHDL Command Reference

#table(
  columns: (20%, 80%), stroke: 0.5pt, inset: 7pt,
  [`ghdl -a`], [Analyze a VHDL source file and place the compiled design unit into the working
  library.],
  [`ghdl -e`], [Elaborate the selected top-level entity and prepare the simulation executable.],
  [`ghdl -r`], [Run a previously elaborated design using GHDL's simulation runtime.],
  [`--std=08`], [Use the VHDL-2008 language standard.],
  [`-o FILE`], [Specify the output simulation executable.],
  [`--vcd=FILE`], [Generate a VCD waveform file during simulation.],
)

